release/RELEASE.md:7:The ordering matters in one direction: old customer versions work with the new ledger, but a new customer version that retries with a new `requestId` and the same `idempotencyKey` requires the new ledger behavior. The customer release should therefore carry the corresponding `deploy_after: ["ledger"]` constraint.
release/RELEASE.md:11:The schema migration runs when a new ledger instance starts, adding the nullable unique `idempotency_key` column at schema version 2. Existing request-ID-only postings remain unchanged. Old customer instances continue sending `requestId` only and are deduplicated as before. New customer instances may send `idempotencyKey`; repeated keys return the original posting and publish no second `payment.posted` event. The shared database and event queue remain usable throughout the rollout.
release/plan.json:2:  "notes": "Deploy ledger fully before deploying the CHG-103 customer release. New ledger instances accept both legacy requestId-only posts and idempotencyKey posts, so old customer instances can run alongside new ledger instances. The customer release must not send retries that depend on idempotency keys until ledger is fully deployed. No drain or atomic switch is required."
